--- !u!114 &-7525753349439422034
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'In this tutorial, you learned how reflections from the environment can be captured and applied onto nearby objects with the help of <b>Reflection Probes.</b>


      For more information, check out the following <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/lighting/reflection-probes.html">documentation.</a>


      <b>Note:</b> You do not need to save your changes in order to follow other tutorials.'
--- !u!114 &-4198700006912007181
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "If an object is not affected by a hand-placed <b>Reflection Probe,</b> it will automatically receive reflections from the Skybox. Therefore, placing Reflection Probes in the Scene is necessary to avoid a phenomenon called \u201Clight leaking\u201D.\n\n1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> select <b>Root</b> > <b>Lighting</b> > <b>Tent</b> > <b>Reflection Probe Tent.</b>\n\n2. Disable <b>Reflection Probe Tent.</b>\n\nOnce disabled, the sky is automatically reflected onto reflective objects, which creates unwanted light leaking.\n\n3. Re-enable <b>Reflection Probe Tent.</b>\n\n4. In the <i>Inspector</i> of <b>Reflection Probe Tent,</b> experiment with the two dedicated shortcut buttons to alter its zone of effect and the capture point of the reflection.\n\n5. Press the <b>Bake</b> button at the bottom of the inspector to re-generate the Reflection Probe.\n\n\n<b>Expert tips</b>\n\nWhen multiple <b>Reflection Probes</b> overlap, you can influence the way they blend by changing their <b>Priority;</b> Reflection Probes with a higher priority will be rendered on top of others."
--- !u!114 &-4149839253865749070
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "A <b>Reflection Probe</b> captures the surrounding environment and stores the result in a texture. These textures are then used to produce per-pixel reflections on objects within the zone of effect of the <b>Reflection Probe.</b> \n\n<b>Reflection Probes</b> are very important to ensure proper material reproduction, notably on materials with a high smoothness or metalness, in interiors and areas that aren\u2019t directly affected by the sky.\n\nIn addition, <b>Reflection Probes</b> can overlap and have a smooth <b>Blend Distance</b> on their sides. Objects will automatically blend between the <b>Reflection Probes</b> based on their position.\n\nFinally, their type can either be <b>Baked</b> or <b>Realtime.</b> The former will bake the results into a texture on disk, whereas the latter will constantly update at runtime to produce true real-time reflections, but at a much higher computational cost. "
